- When `counter` reaches 4, it resets to 0, indicating a new transition has occurred.
- You can add any additional logic inside the `if` block to handle the specific behavior when a transition happens.

This setup ensures that there will be exactly one transition every 5 clock cycles, which corresponds to 5 transitions per 32-bit number (assuming each bit change counts as a transition). Adjust the timing parameters (`#5`) according to your requirements.

