If you need more control over the processes spawned by coroutines, you can use `pcntl_fork` along with process control functions like `posix_setsid`, `posix_setpgid`, etc.

```php
function runCoroutine($job) {
    $pid = pcntl_fork();
    if ($pid == -1) {
        die('Could not fork');
    } elseif ($pid) {
        // Parent process
        posix_setsid(); // Create a new session
        posix_setpgid(0, 0); // Set the process group ID
    } else {
        // Child process
        // Your coroutine logic here
        exit;
    }
}

// Example usage
